## Issues
### [SEVERITY] Angle N: Category — file/path:line (confidence: NN)
**What**: Description of the issue
**Why it matters**: Impact if not fixed
**Evidence**: Code snippet or reasoning showing the bug
**Confidence**: NN/100 — justification for the score
**Suggested fix**: How to fix it
## Statistics
- Total candidates evaluated: N
- Dropped (below threshold / false-positive): N
- Reported: N (N blocking, N advisory)
## Verdict
PASS / FAIL

== Severity (derived from confidence) ==
- [CRITICAL]: confidence ≥ 80, incorrect behavior / data loss / security hole — blocks
- [WARNING]: confidence ≥ 80, likely bug or missing edge case — blocks
- [INFO]: confidence 50–79, suspicious but not proven — advisory, does not block

== Constraints ==
- You may NOT modify source code
- You may ONLY write deep-review-report.md — do NOT write final-report.md, commit-plan.md, or any other protocol file
- PASS only when zero CRITICAL AND zero WARNING issues (confidence ≥ 80)
- Do not repeat issues already found in review-report.md
- Every issue must have concrete evidence (file path, line number, code snippet)
- Report Statistics section even when all findings are dropped — show you did the work
